  "development_findings": [
    "Rejected invalid fragment owner initially dereferenced a null source name; validation now handles it.",
    "Creation-frame zero elapsed time originally produced a zero-length collision ray; explicitly skip it without weakening the ray service.",
    "Sustained retail alternate Flare fire exposed a detached limb starting inside train geometry. Reuse bounded nonsolid-body placement with a parent anchor before physics. Original flare.private passes without changes to that test.",
    "Old corpse and weapon-drop tests expected unavailable fire/gib services; they now assert actual lethal behavior, source removal intent, gib publication and preserved drop ordering.",
    "Final Debug character GPU smoke lost desktop window focus at frame 50, so its crouch/run assertions failed. The unchanged focused test was rerun independently; initial failure and rerun logs retained.",
    "Source smoke STREAMING combines MOVINGSOURCE/MOVINGSTREAM; a stationary smoke source emits no particles. Explicit moving-source CPU/GPU probes verify its actual recipe."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Tests combine original external assets with diagnostic placements; this is not a complete retail playthrough.",
